            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erin M"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was excellent! I did modify slightly. I used chicken breasts cut into bite-sized pieces. I could not find mochiko (didn't have time to go to an Asian market), but I followed the directions otherwise- except subbed teriyaki for the oyster sauce- and then just before frying, I tossed the pieces with Panko. The whole family loved it- this will go on my 'make often' list for sure!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cookin Up A Storm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good. The directions are a little sketchy on exactly how the whole dredging thing is supposed to happen, but what I did was leave the Rice Flour out of the \"marinade\" and use that to do the pre-fry dredge. Not sure if that was the intention, but it made for a nice crispy and light coating on this tasty chicken. I will definitely make this again. I did this recipe as a part of the Western Region's Faceless Frenzy July 2012.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-01T18:09:12.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
